# KSU_Builder dev Branch License
## Overview
This license applies specifically to the **dev** branch of the **KSU_Builder** repository. This branch contains custom GitHub Actions workflows, build automation scripts, and documentation created for custom builds and advanced deployments. **Use with caution and at your own risk.**
---
## Terms and Conditions
### 1. Purpose
The dev branch is provided as-is for:
- Testing new build workflows and automation
- Evaluation of build system improvements
- Experimentation with different kernel configurations
- Development and deployment of custom features
### 2. Usage Restrictions
Users of this dev branch agree to:
- Not use in production without thorough testing and validation on your specific hardware
- Test thoroughly before deploying any artifacts built from this branch to end-user devices
- Report issues with clear reproduction steps and environment details
- Verify compatibility with your specific kernel source, device, and toolchain before use
### 3. Disclaimer of Warranty
THIS DEV BRANCH IS PROVIDED "AS IS" WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO:
- FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE
- MERCHANTABILITY
- NON-INFRINGEMENT
- PERFORMANCE
- RELIABILITY
- STABILITY
The workflows, scripts, and documentation on this branch are experimental and may:
- Produce broken or non-functional builds
- Have incomplete error handling
- Change significantly without notice 
- Fail without clear error messages
- Consume excessive resources
### 4. Limitation of Liability
In no event shall the authors, contributors, or repository maintainers be liable for:
- Bricked devices or data loss resulting from builds created with this branch
- Failed kernel compilations or APK builds
- Telegram notification failures
- Resource exhaustion or billing issues from GitHub Actions
- Incompatibility with your kernel source or device configuration
- Any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages
### 5. Upstream Compliance
Where applicable, this dev branch maintains compatibility with:
- The official KernelSU project (https://github.com/tiann/KernelSU)
- All upstream licenses and terms
For upstream project licensing, refer to the main/master branch and the KernelSU project's original license.
### 6. Artifact Warranties
Artifacts built from this dev branch (kernel ZIPs, APKs, binaries) are:
- Provided as-is and tested only as of the present date
- Not signed with production certificates
- Not guaranteed to be secure or free of vulnerabilities
- Subject to change between builds without notice
### 7. Testing Obligations
By using this dev branch, you acknowledge:
- You will test thoroughly before installation on any device
- You will backup your data before flashing any builds
- You understand risks of using custom and experimental software
- You will not hold maintainers responsible for issues arising from use
### 8. Feedback and Reporting
If you use this dev branch and discover issues:
- Report with clear reproduction steps and error logs
- Include your device, kernel source, and toolchain information
- Provide verbose workflow logs from GitHub Actions
- Use respectful, constructive language
Reported issues help improve stability, but reporting does not guarantee fixes or support.
### 9. No Support Guarantee
Usage of this dev branch does not guarantee:
- Technical support or assistance
- Bug fixes or patches
- Response to issues or PRs
- Maintenance or updates
Support is provided on a best-effort basis by volunteers.
### 10. Modifications and Distribution
You may:
- Fork this branch and modify workflows for personal use
- Create PRs with improvements
- Share experiences and feedback
You may not:
- Claim this branch as your own work
- Distribute modified versions without attribution
- Remove or alter this license
- Misrepresent this as official production-ready software
### 11. Branch Status
This dev branch is considered:
- Experimental — features and workflows may change
- Unstable — compatibility not guaranteed
- Unsupported — use at your own discretion and at your own risk
- Dynamic — may be rebased, reset, or updated without notice
### 12. Acknowledgment of Risks
Users acknowledge understanding that:
- Kernel compilation is complex and error-prone
- Automated builds can fail silently
- Telegram notifications may not indicate actual build status
- GitHub Actions have rate limits and resource constraints
- Build artifacts may be incomplete or corrupted
### 13. Third-Party Software
This branch uses and integrates with:
- AOSP Clang (https://android.googlesource.com/platform/prebuilts/clang/)
- KernelSU (https://github.com/Justadeayo/KernelSU)
- AnyKernel3 (https://github.com/Justadeayo/AnyKernel3)
- GitHub Actions (https://github.com/features/actions)
- Other open-source tools
Refer to upstream projects for their respective licenses and terms.
